  "summary": "The City of Charlotte issued an RFP on September 9 seeking a new ALPR system to replace the one CMPD has used for over a decade. The RFP calls for centralized management, data retention, real-time alerting, and vehicle analytics, and closes October 5. CMPD does not own Flock cameras in Charlotte but has access agreements with Flock.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "CMPD has used its current ALPR system for more than a decade, and as technology, related equipment, and operational needs have evolved, the department initiated a competitive procurement process to ensure the next platform meets modern public safety capabilities",
      "paragraph_idx": 6
    },
    {
      "quote": "CMPD does not own or operate any of the Flock cameras in Charlotte but has agreements in place that allow officers to access Flock databases.",
      "paragraph_idx": 11
    }
